# Canonical docs ↔ HTML twins (hard)

## Sources of truth

| Canonical (master) | Visual twin (not master) |
|---|---|
| `docs/roadmap/roadmap.md` | `docs/erp/status/roadmap.html` |
| `docs/architecture/project-structure.md` | `docs/erp/status/project-structure.html` |

HTML under `docs/erp/status/` is a **report only**. Never invent progress only in HTML. Never leave MD updated and HTML stale.

## Atomic write (same iteration)

If you change **any** of: checkbox `[x]`/`[ ]`, microtask code, title, note/evidence, dependencies, stage/block note, new/removed microtask — you **must** update the HTML twin in the **same** edit pass before the iteration report.

Forbidden:

- Close MD `- [x] CODE` and leave HTML `done: false` (or missing `code`).
- Flip HTML `done` without the matching MD checkbox.
- Update only Stage/item **notes** in HTML while checkbox/`done` flags stay wrong.
- Defer “HTML sync” to a follow-up iteration.
- Add a microtask in one file only.

## Mapping rules

- Roadmap MD `- [x] CODE — …` ↔ HTML microtask `{ code: "CODE", done: true, note?: "…" }`.
- Roadmap MD `- [ ] CODE — …` ↔ HTML `done: false`.
- Same `CODE` string on both sides (e.g. `8.2.2.6`).
- When MD has evidence after the em dash, HTML should carry a short `note` (version / path / task file).
- Parent section headings in MD may lack a checkbox; progress lives on microtasks. Do not invent a fake parent `done` in HTML unless MD has a matching checkbox.
- Allowed HTML-only stubs: archival markers with a clear suffix (e.g. `6.1.13.moved`) that are **not** progress checkboxes — do not use them to mark unfinished work done.

## End-of-iteration gate

Before reporting done on any roadmap/checklist change:

1. Diff both MD and HTML twin paths.
2. Spot-check every code you closed or reopened: MD state ≡ HTML `done`.
3. In the report write **`HTML twin synced`** (name the files) or list mismatches and fix them first.
4. Treat MD↔HTML desync of closed items as **P1 process** — stop and repair; do not advance the next microtask.

